        "statement": "Let $R$ be a commutative ring, $q\\in R^{\\times}$, and let $H=H_{R,q}(S_n)$ be the specialized type-A Hecke algebra with generators $T_1,\\dots,T_{n-1}$ and relations $T_i^2=(q-1)T_i+q$, the braid relations and the distant commutations ([[def-generic-type-a-hecke-algebra]], [[thm-standard-basis-of-the-generic-type-a-hecke-algebra]]). Then the assignment $T_i\\mapsto T_i$ ($1\\le i<n$) extends uniquely to an $R$-algebra anti-automorphism $*:H\\to H$, i.e. an $R$-linear map with $(ab)^*=b^*a^*$ and $1^*=1$; it is an involution, $**=\\mathrm{id}_H$, and on the standard basis $$T_w^{*}=T_{w^{-1}}\\qquad(w\\in S_n).$$ In particular $(T_wT_{w^{-1}})^*=T_wT_{w^{-1}}$ and, for the symmetrizers $m_\\lambda=\\sum_{w\\in S_\\lambda}T_w$, one has $m_\\lambda^*=m_\\lambda$.",
