        "title": "The type-A quantum algebra and its tensor-action formulas",
        "statement": "Let $F=\\mathbb Q(q)$ with $q$ an indeterminate, let $N\\ge1$, and put $K_i=L_iL_{i+1}^{-1}$ for $1\\le i<N$. Start with the free associative $F$-algebra on $L_j,L_j^{-1}$ ($1\\le j\\le N$) and $E_i,F_i$ ($1\\le i<N$), and quotient by the two-sided ideal generated by the following relations:\n\n1. $L_jL_j^{-1}=L_j^{-1}L_j=1$ and $L_jL_k=L_kL_j$ for all $j,k$.\n2. $L_jE_iL_j^{-1}=q^{\\delta_{j,i}-\\delta_{j,i+1}}E_i$ and $L_jF_iL_j^{-1}=q^{-\\delta_{j,i}+\\delta_{j,i+1}}F_i$.\n3. $[E_i,F_j]=\\delta_{ij}(K_i-K_i^{-1})/(q-q^{-1})$.\n4. $[E_i,E_j]=[F_i,F_j]=0$ when $|i-j|>1$.\n5. For $|i-j|=1$, $E_i^2E_j-(q+q^{-1})E_iE_jE_i+E_jE_i^2=0$ and $F_i^2F_j-(q+q^{-1})F_iF_jF_i+F_jF_i^2=0$.\n\nHere $[x,y]=xy-yx$. The free algebra and quotient construction are those of [[lem-hh-free-associative-ring-and-relations-descent]]; this definition asserts existence of the presented associative algebra, not the well-definedness of structural maps on its quotient.\n\nOn $V_N$ with ordered basis $e_1,\\ldots,e_N$, prescribe the candidate matrices\n$$L_je_a=q^{\\delta_{ja}}e_a,\\qquad E_ie_a=\\delta_{a,i+1}e_i,\\qquad F_ie_a=\\delta_{a,i}e_{i+1}.$$\nPrescribe candidate coproduct and counit values by\n$$\\Delta(L_j)=L_j\\otimes L_j,\\quad \\Delta(E_i)=E_i\\otimes K_i+1\\otimes E_i,\\quad \\Delta(F_i)=F_i\\otimes1+K_i^{-1}\\otimes F_i,$$\nand $\\epsilon(L_j^{\\pm1})=1$, $\\epsilon(E_i)=\\epsilon(F_i)=0$. The following relation-descent lemma proves that these assignments define the vector representation and bialgebra structure, and hence the tensor actions used below.",
