        "title": "Polynomial quantum Schur first levels: Weyl filtration and the actual Hecke corner",
        "statement": "Put $A=\\mathbb Z[v,v^{-1}]$, $q=v^2$, and use the actual integral tensor action and the finite normalized-cell constructions of [[lem-integral-divided-power-tensor-action-surjects-onto-type-a-q-schur-algebra]] and [[lem-integral-quantum-highest-weight-modules-identify-with-normalized-q-schur-weyl-cells]]. For $N>d\\ge1$, $\\lambda\\vdash d$, and $W_N(\\lambda)$ its Weyl module, the **first level** is $W_N(\\lambda)^1=\\bigoplus_{\\alpha_N=1}W_N(\\lambda)_\\alpha$. It has an integral lower-Schur Weyl filtration with one factor $W_{N-1}(\\lambda(i))$ for each removable row $i$, ordered by decreasing dominance of $\\lambda(i)$. This filtration and its quotient identifications commute with arbitrary coefficient-ring base change.\n\nOver every field with a chosen unit $v$, write $\\nabla=W^\\tau$ and $L=W/\\operatorname{rad}B_\\tau$, with the suppliers' abstract highest norm-one form. Then $\\operatorname{Hom}(W_{N-1}(\\mu),\\nabla_N(\\lambda)^1)$ is one dimensional exactly for $\\mu=\\lambda(i)$, and zero otherwise. The same Hom-space with target $L_N(\\lambda)^1$ has dimension at most one and vanishes off these labels. Equivalently every lower-Levi primitive line of $L_N(\\lambda)^1$ has one of these weights, with dimension at most one; primitive means annihilated by **all** positive divided generators.\n\nFor every commutative ring $R$, unit $q$, and left $S_R(N,d)$-module $V$, its first level carries the actual lower algebra $S_R(N-1,d-1)$ action induced on permutation modules, and there is a natural isomorphism\n$$e_{\\rm lower}V^1\\cong\\operatorname{Res}^{H_d}_{H_{d-1}}eV.$$\nThe quantum Levi action, when a square root is chosen, agrees with this action under the actual tensor identification and the suppliers' weight-unit conjugation. This statement neither equates first level with a simple-root layer nor asserts that an exact corner functor preserves socles.",
